From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:50:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Raise the m68k default task stack to match the other targets

16 KB made m68k the outlier in this tree by a factor of two and a half:
i386, ppc, riscv and x86_64 all use 40960, MorphOS 32768, m68k 16384. It is
a figure from machines with 512 KB of RAM in them, and this target has 840 MB.

It is also not enough. With a frame validator in the scheduler,
WANDERER:Wanderer was caught writing its persistent task frame below
tc_SPLower -- outside its own stack -- 97 times in one boot. Everything the
scheduler saved and restored from there belonged to something else, which is
why pointers read back out of it were fragments of strings.

Measured at 64 KB, deliberately above every other target so the test had
headroom: validator reports went from 97 in a run to zero across eight, and
runaway exception recursion from one to none. Landed at 40960, because
agreeing with the other targets is a better argument than any number chosen
for this port.

It does not change the boot rate; that was measured too, and said so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h
+++ b/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h
@@ -116,7 +116,24 @@
     Not so much, I think (schulz) ;-))
 */
 
-#define AROS_STACKSIZE  0x4000
+/*
+ * 16 KB made m68k the outlier in this tree by a factor of two and a half:
+ *
+ *     i386-all     40960      ppc-all      40960
+ *     riscv-all    40960      x86_64-all   40960
+ *     ppc-morphos  32768      m68k-all     16384
+ *
+ * It is a figure from machines with 512 KB of RAM in them, and this target has
+ * 840 MB. With a frame validator in the scheduler, WANDERER:Wanderer was caught
+ * writing its persistent task frame below tc_SPLower -- outside its own stack
+ * -- 97 times in one boot, after which everything the scheduler saved and
+ * restored belonged to something else. See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0014.md.
+ *
+ * 40960 matches every target here that is not MorphOS. The measurement that
+ * justified raising it at all was taken at 64 KB, deliberately above them so
+ * the test had headroom to walk back from.
+ */
+#define AROS_STACKSIZE  0xA000
 
 //#define AROS_NEEDS___MAIN
 
